description: TILA agent memory — selective context + append task-history
alwaysApply: true
---

Agents do not remember chats. Prior work lives in `docs/brain/`. ADRs live in `docs/decisions/`.

Before a feature task:
1. Resolve docs via `docs/context-routing.json` (skill: `.agents/skills/tila-context/SKILL.md`). Load only `default` + matched `always` (optional when needed).
2. Read `docs/brain/roadmap.md`, `docs/brain/gaps.md`.
3. Read or create `docs/brain/task-history/<feature-slug>.md` (copy `_TEMPLATE.md`).
4. Prefer `/StartTask` then `/MakePlan` before coding.
5. Skim `docs/architecture/dependency-map.md` when changing Auth, gateway, embeddings, workers, or shared core.

After finishing (or when asked to hand off):
1. Append an entry to the task-history file (never rewrite history).
2. Update roadmap/gaps; write new ADRs under `docs/decisions/`.
3. Prefer `/Handoff` (after `/ReviewCode` and `/TestCode` when implementing).

Skill: `.agents/skills/tila-memory/SKILL.md`.
